  "strategy": "1. **Approach and Rationale**\nThe provided parent solution shows promise with a C5 value of 0.380989. Further improvement requires escaping local optima and leveraging multiple representations. The current algorithm uses iterative refinement from an initial guess, which may be suboptimal. We will introduce:\n- Multiple initial representations (parent, smoothed parent, binary-like)\n- Stricter maintenance of integral constraints\n- Coarser resolution optimization before refinement\n- Strategic use of binary restarts\n- Progressive refinement with constraint projection\n\nThis addresses two main limitations: (a) the parent solution might be locally optimal, (b) gradient-based optimization may fail for non-convex problems.\n\nKey improvements include:\n- Step-based binary initialization for population-based search\n- New constraint enforcement through projection\n- Variable neighborhood exploration\n- Independent vs interpolation approaches\n\n2. **Mathematical Specification**\n**Variables:** h \u2208 [0,1]^{n} with sum(h) = n/2\n**Objective:** Minimize C5(h) = max_k (1/dx) \u222b h(x)\u00b7(1-h(x+k)) dx\n**Constraints:**\n- 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1 for all i\n- sum(h) = n/2\n**Resolution handling:** Maintain feasibility across n changes\n\n3. **Implementation Procedure**\n**Parent Validation:**\n- If initial_h_values exists, use as base population\n- Else generate uniform [0,1] vector and project sum to n/2\n\n**Step-like Binary Representation:**\n  - Start with h[i] \u2208 {0.25, 0.5, 0.75}\n  - Adjust to meet sum(h) = n/2 while keeping binary-like structure\n\n**Constraint Enforcement:**\n  - Define enforce_sum(h) to adjust values via weighted averaging\n  - Implement clip_and_project(): clip values, then adjust sum by modifying extreme values\n\n**Mixed Strategy Optimization:**\n**Phase 1: Exploration**\n- Generate candidates through:\n  - Mutation (random walk near best)\n  - Binary restart (random 0/1 with sum n/2)\n  - Coarse resolution (n=60) with scaled parent values\n**Phase 2: Exploitation**\n- Progressive refinement (n=120,240,360)\n- Successive orthogonal projections to nearest feasible point\n- Budget-aware annealing schedule (\u223c5-20 seconds per anealing sweep)\n\n4. **Search Choices**\n**Initial Configurations:**\n- Try 5-10 diverse structures:\n  1. Parent clone (direct search)\n  2. Localized smooth parent\n  3. Binary step parent\n  4. Alternating pattern\n  5. Random walk initialization\n- Dynamic resolution: start at 120 samples, then 240,360\n\n**Hyperparameter Scheduling:**\n- Temperature schedule: {300,1000,3000,10000} (Gaussian noise scale)\n- Restart budget: 200 seconds total per phase\n- Intermittent binary restarts (\u223c10% of candidates)\n\n**Adaptive Component:**\n- Budget monitoring through wall clock checks\n- Dynamic dimensionality: allow pruning of new dimensions\n\n5. **Budget & Performance**\n- Phase 1: 10 seconds (exploration)\n- Phase 2: 800 seconds (sequential refinement)\n- Resolution changes: 3 stages (60/120/180/240)\n- Fail-safe: Return best valid candidate even if budget exhausted\n\n6. **Validation & Output**\n- After each full resolution cycle, evaluate C5 for non-dominated candidates\n- Final projection ensures sum(h) = n/2 with clipping/adjustment\n- Return best_h, best_c5, and effective_n",
